% This means that during the duration of one time slot, the UAV maintains a fixed horizontal location, enabling stable communication links and sensing operations.
Across different time slots, the UAVs fly to the next position, e.g., the position of the $ k $-th L-UAV in time slot $ l $ is expressed as \({\bf{q}}_k[l+1] = (q_k^x{[l+1]}, q_k^y{[l+1]}, H)\).\footnote{We assume that the L-UAVs conduct LAE tasks in the flying region, with their positions known across all time slots. Meanwhile, the position of the U-UAV can be estimated via surveillance systems. The goal of the DFBS is to maximize U-UAV sensing precision for ensuring the L-UAV mission safety and securing their data transmission services.}
