The macroscopic computational domain is discretized using 656 eight-node hexahedral elements, while each microscopic domain employs 10 linear interval elements. To validate \texttt{DiffLiB}'s accuracy in 3D analysis, we compare the prediction results against \texttt{COMSOL}.

