\section{Edge-Assisted VR System Model}\label{sec:system}
As depicted in Fig. \ref{fig:system-model}, we consider a multi-user $360^\circ$ VR video streaming application with $N$ users  
% The videos are stored in an ECU located in the proximity of an indoor VR arena.
that are equipped with VR headsets and  connected to an ECU through  mmWave wireless links.
% The ECU streams various $360^\circ$ videos to users.
All VR headsets and the ECU are equipped with computational resources (\ie CPU and GPU) to decode/render multi-layer $360^\circ$ videos, as described next. 
% Next, we explain multi-layer $360^\circ$ video model and how the $360^\circ$ videos are stored in ECU. 
