\textbf{VR Headset Decoding and Rendering Model:}
We incorporate a decoding and rendering model developed by \cite{Chakareski-2023-Millimeter} to compute the decoding and rendering time for each GoP.
In this model, the decoding time of the $m^{th}$ GoP for the $n^{th}$ user is assessed as $\Tilde{si}(e^m_n)/ \bar{Z}^{dec.}_n$, where $\Tilde{si}(.)$ returns the decoding computational complexity of a GoP, in bits, which is the induced data rate associated with the current viewport and the quality of the streamed video (\ie $\Tilde{si}(e^m_n) = d(e^m_n)$).
% given the video bitrate and the user's viewport information.
Similarly, the rendering time is modeled as $si(e^m_n)/ \bar{Z}^{rend.}_n$, where $si(.)$ returns the rendering computational complexity of a GoP, in bits, which is the induced data rate after decoding of the GoP (\ie $si(e^m_n) = d(e^m_n) / \beta$).
Note that we assume that the viewport information is available on the headset.

