\subsection{Insights and Limitations}

RL enables forecast-free deployment and adapts well to uncertainty, but it requires extensive training and tuning. In contrast, LP offers interpretability and robust solutions but is less flexible under uncertain conditions. Therefore, hybrid approaches could take the advantages of both methods. Although LP with perfect forecasts outperforms RL, the later remains valuable when forecasts fail or are unreliable. Therefore, future work should compare forecasting methods to gain more insights into the respective control capabilities. Additionally, the multi criteria based objective and reward functions design requires further study in terms of a sensitivity analysis for the weights attached to individual objectives. In terms of simulation modeling, replacing average temperature models with higher-fidelity thermal or more accurate electrochemical battery models for SOC estimation could enhance the accuracy of the system states estimation.


