The system setup includes a vertically arranged configuration in which the PAT is directed downward towards the liquid medium (Figure \ref{explanation}). A parallel light source is created using a point LED light source, which is then collimated by a Fresnel lens to produce uniform illumination from below the tank. As the ultrasound waves emitted by the PAT interact with the liquid surface, they generate acoustic pressure fields that deform the surface, leading to the formation of caustic patterns when the light is refracted by these deformations. The acoustic pressure induces concave deformations on the liquid surface. As shown in Figure \ref{mechanism} (b), these concave surfaces bend light outward, generating shadows. In Figure \ref{mechanism} (c), a single focal point of acoustic pressure deforms the surface, resulting in a caustic pattern with a dark center, surrounded by light focused outward. 

