\subsection{YOLO11 Network Architecture}

The detection backbone in this study is the lightweight You Only Look Once version 11 (YOLO11) network, an evolution of the YOLOv5/YOLOv8 family that balances inference speed with high detection accuracy. YOLO11 adopts a CSP–Ghost backbone for efficient feature reuse, incorporates depthwise separable convolutions to reduce parameter count, and employs a decoupled head with separate branches for classification, bounding box regression, and objectness scores. For the segmentation variant (YOLO11n-seg), a lightweight decoder with panoptic feature aggregation is appended to generate pixel wise masks while sharing the majority of the detection backbone. The network was trained end-to-end with mosaic augmentation, CIoU loss for bounding boxes, and binary cross-entropy for mask predictions. Figure~\ref{fig:yolo11_arch} illustrates the high level architecture adopted in this work. Full implementation details and source code are available in the official repository \cite{yolo11github}.

