\subsection{Symbolic Finite Protocols} 
Finally, we study symbolic representations of finite protocols. More precisely, we consider the fragment of symbolic protocols where $\MsgVals$ is the set of Booleans and all transition constraints~$\varphi$ are given by propositional formulas. 
We show that for this class of symbolic protocols, the implementability problem is PSPACE-complete. 
